<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:59:10Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>South African former police chief accused of sex trafficking denied bail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54f1ce9ccf89eb91a894f918777f0f618fd5a0a2ed99564f8adb98d11d27b1d4</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:44:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-south-african-former-police-chief-accused-of-sex-trafficking-denied-bail--532cffa65e7a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-south-african-former-police-chief-accused-of-sex-trafficking-denied-bail" /><summary type="html">South Africa's former deputy national commissioner, Shadrack Sibiya, has been denied bail. He is facing charges of rape, trafficking and is accused of sexually grooming a child. Investigators had argued that his accusers would be in danger if he was let out. FRANCE 24's correspondent Eunice Masson reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: French union leaders urges strikes after meeting with PM Lecornu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39701bdbbbeb954297eb43ed4f736ae97d80c80fe88bd4b3728233d85717fca2</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:30:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-french-union-leaders-urges-strikes-after-meeting-with-pm-lecornu--2db9f2740c05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-french-union-leaders-urges-strikes-after-meeting-with-pm-lecornu" /><summary type="html">The leader of France's hardline CGT union on Wednesday called for strikes after talks with Prime Minister Sebastien Lecornu over fresh protests collapsed. As the country is reeling from last weekend's riots, the government offered "no measure or an acknowledgement of our demands" Sophie Binet, secretary general of the CGT, told reporters after a meeting between Lecornu and union leaders.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nigeria records its first Ebola case amid rapid regional spread</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04ee747b6b64d71cfbf1be5d8e548058ad6d45f8cf36f9525d54094cc3d5a38d</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:28:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-amid-rapid-regional-spread--6d9583291599.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-nigeria-records-its-first-ebola-case-amid-rapid-regional-spread" /><summary type="html">After Kenya and Uganda, Nigeria has now announced its first Ebola case – a woman who was admitted to a private hospital in Abuja and travelled from Uganda. The outbreak, which originated in DR Congo in May, has been described by health officials as ​thefastest-spreading on record. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent Sam Olukoya.</summary></entry><entry><title>What makes a great Halloween cake?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f5d77e7c319cd1c9c9437b1ca6c4f0526ed3249c14fc8d2b2ac5c6cae6a0c61</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261021-what-makes-a-great-halloween-cake--0d3f26bad8aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261021-what-makes-a-great-halloween-cake" /><summary type="html">With Halloween around the corner we are pleased to welcome cake decoration expert Galina Duverne from the École de Cake Design in Paris. Galina tells us what makes a great Halloween cake and how the French have slowly been seduced by cake decorating.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>US sanctions on ICC are 'a shock' and 'unacceptable', Nobel peace laureate Navi Pillay says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a896e401519b8ad4ec7135e1e335793b26cc81a37860e1bcf93616f880b46e12</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:11:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261021-us-sanctions-on-icc-are-a-shock-and-unacceptable-nobel-peace-laureate-navi-pillay-says--b2b2f9ec09fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261021-us-sanctions-on-icc-are-a-shock-and-unacceptable-nobel-peace-laureate-navi-pillay-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Nobel Peace Prize laureate Navi Pillay described the US sanctions imposed on the International Criminal Court (ICC) hours after her award as "a shock" and "unacceptable". The South African judge also defended the UN commission of inquiry she chaired which concluded that Israel had committed genocide in Gaza: "We didn't come to that conclusion lightly." Rejecting claims that the ICC targets Africa, she said "the court is not selective".</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Portugal police clear demonstrators from protest camps against cost of housing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d35db2a17ef6c7a6c3bd9b1e0baa7133521642411ffced1423931d35dd0fbcf</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T12:31:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-portugal-police-clear-demonstrators-from-protest-camps-against-cost-of-housing--71256b40ecc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-portugal-police-clear-demonstrators-from-protest-camps-against-cost-of-housing" /><summary type="html">Portuguese demonstrators have been protesting against the cost of housing in the country. They are opposed to recent measures announced by the government and are calling for a new gathering in the coming days, despite police clearing protest camps.</summary></entry><entry><title>Visual artist Amadeo Carvalho explores Black identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e4f200732995ba9adfbc1793c5330e610b2f9f8f78b7e8e1602dbc82143a288</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T12:21:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261021-visual-artist-amadeo-carvalho-explores-black-identity--a7a9e973aebb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261021-visual-artist-amadeo-carvalho-explores-black-identity" /><summary type="html">From Cape Verde to London and beyond, Amadeo Carvalho is a self-taught, London-based contemporary visual artist putting Black identity, memory and heritage at the heart of his work. Blending painting, poetry and photography, his art explores the stories, silences and connections that shape who we are. This weekend, his powerful collection "Portraits of Absence" arrives at the AKAA Art Fair here in Paris, where it will be exhibited by the curatorial platform Casa Vicência. He spoke to us in Perspective</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>'Who are the vandals?' ask the French press after weekend riots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52d090dd999513b6189a9dadc8b62e434214d830eeb204b768d929ff94fe42b3</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T12:07:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261021-who-are-the-vandals-ask-the-french-press-after-weekend-riots--e0f6d4227345.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261021-who-are-the-vandals-ask-the-french-press-after-weekend-riots" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, October 21: The identities of some 300 suspects from Saturday's riots are emerging in the Paris courts. Meanwhile, the far-left France Unbowed party has promised legal action against the French government for claiming the radical left was responsible for the degeneration of protests. Also, as the UN warns that global warming is on track to reach 2.6°C this century, the UK greenlights new drilling in the North Sea. Finally, we look at the literary trend of hate-reading.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Macron says world leaders have made 'stupid' comments on France riots based on fake AI videos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed80b3c3d998e89e182654622c866029ba44a93c458c20df4ff34987cfb54f30</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T11:48:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261021-macron-says-world-leaders-have-made-stupid-comments-on-france-riots-based-on-fake-ai-videos--3243562e20d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261021-macron-says-world-leaders-have-made-stupid-comments-on-france-riots-based-on-fake-ai-videos" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron took aim at world leaders including US President Donald Trump for trying to exploit the riots and looting that broke out alongside peaceful demonstrations in France Saturday for their own political advantage. Another wave of demonstrations against France's worsening cost of living is planned for the coming Saturday.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>US envoy Steve Witkoff thanks Vladimir Putin for diesel deal at Ukraine talks in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27a9267026f5781eee12540540d20c91c8a768aed5c64c10f80f0614206e924e</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T11:07:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-envoy-steve-witkoff-thanks-vladimir-putin-for-diesel-deal-at-ukraine-talks-in-russia--30521be1972e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-envoy-steve-witkoff-thanks-vladimir-putin-for-diesel-deal-at-ukraine-talks-in-russia" /><summary type="html">US envoy Steve Witkoff is in Saint Petersburg, holding talks with Russian president Vladimir Putin. The face to face meeting comes after he met with Ukraine's president and other European leaders in Oslo. Witkoff is due to return to the Norwegian capital after his visit to Russia. Washington seeks to breathe new life into US-led efforts to end the war. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor, Kethevane Gorjestani.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine talks: US envoy meets Vladimir Putin in Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b7d2053d7d3849706888f6984b4015d033afc39ba8bded7f6ef72da5eeed847</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T11:04:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-us-envoy-meets-vladimir-putin-in-russia--fcf1a297b9ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-us-envoy-meets-vladimir-putin-in-russia" /><summary type="html">US envoy Steve Witkoff held talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin in St. Petersburg on Wednesday about Moscow’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine, as US President Donald Trump pushes Kyiv to make a deal that stops the fighting. The day before, the American official had met with Ukraine's Volodymyr Zelensky in Oslo, Norway. Details by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Philip Turle.</summary></entry><entry><title>Egypt mulls joining Saudi Arabia in war against Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4871ca9d534ab055f4a02a8a5793650661d000387e1fe7f50390238e95c4cc6e</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T11:02:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/egypt-mulls-joining-saudi-arabia-in-war-against-houthis--71c10c680ac4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/egypt-mulls-joining-saudi-arabia-in-war-against-houthis" /><summary type="html">Egypt may be about to join the war against Houthis. Saudi Arabia has come under sustained attack from the Iran-backed group in recent weeks after a collapse of a truce in Yemen in September. Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman visited Egypt mid-September to request potential military support from the country – a demand put before parliament by the Egyptian president on Saturday. Story by Camille Corcoran.</summary></entry><entry><title>Musk talks up potential merger of SpaceX and Tesla</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eddf3e19fc6afedc8ebaa78fbe745ed43c7cce55e2619e8025af474cc89d7ad2</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T10:26:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261021-musk-talks-up-potential-merger-of-spacex-and-tesla--7ec07fc0e542.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20261021-musk-talks-up-potential-merger-of-spacex-and-tesla" /><summary type="html">As SpaceX reports blockbuster quarterly earnings, CEO Elon Musk floats the possibility of merging the rocketry and AI firm with his electric car company Tesla. Also in this edition: OpenAI reveals more agent misbehaviour as market turmoil hits data centre companies, and France's political crisis exacerbates its bond market rout.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>French Prime Minister vows 'massive' police deployment for new demonstrations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdc45e4de1c18d3d4a927a2cc9d7c918347a1b9349cc5064a8aa638d63a43f8b</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T10:25:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-french-prime-minister-vows-massive-police-deployment-for-new-demonstrations--97320fe10cce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-french-prime-minister-vows-massive-police-deployment-for-new-demonstrations" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu has vowed a "massive" police deployment for the fresh demonstrations called for Saturday by the "Yellow Vest" movement. Facing angry lawmakers in parliament, Lecornu acknowledged that the security response had fallen short and promised a stronger approach ahead of this new wave of protests.</summary></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: French president addresses fuel supplies during Gulf tour</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0449c74dddbb139e4d0d8630e03f433ca62f22f5d5260ece5c67832928b1abe</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T10:18:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/replay-french-president-addresses-fuel-supplies-during-gulf-tour--340b4074fa18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/replay-french-president-addresses-fuel-supplies-during-gulf-tour" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron said on Tuesday he had secured the delivery of an additional 200,000 tonnes of diesel per month from the United Arab Emirates and Bahrain. He is currently in Doha as part of a tour of the Gulf. "We are reducing our dependency" he said whilst speaking to the press on October 21.</summary></entry><entry><title>Italy deploys troops into Milan in response to recent riots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48577edb20b30069a1cf069ea9189a99fc532f430dfcee80942939d5c5e49baa</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T10:08:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-italy-deploys-troops-into-milan-in-response-to-recent-riots--84aa1e97f2c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-italy-deploys-troops-into-milan-in-response-to-recent-riots" /><summary type="html">Italy approved troop deployment after intense riots in Milan. Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni toughened security laws after clashes between youths and the police, following a weekend of unrest in several Italian cities. FRANCE 24's correspondent Seema Gupta reports from the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine talks: What progress after US envoy met with Zelensky?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f672b5ecb4b085d5ab41b2a34167a0a1dd7232ababc3ffef560ccdedf79e7de1</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T09:58:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-what-progress-after-us-envoy-met-with-zelensky--e9f78446a0bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-what-progress-after-us-envoy-met-with-zelensky" /><summary type="html">US Special Envoy Steve Witkoff is headed to Russia today to meet with Russian President Vladimir Putin for peace talks. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, on his end, met with the US official in Norway Tuesday. What progress has been made in Oslo? Ophélie Jacobson explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Russia releases US citizen accused of fighting for Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0ecdfc127e1055c7c0d24f7179d25fa85a701cd6e10028bc838f35d2df64c88</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T09:21:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-us-envoy-witkoff-to-meet-putin-in-russia-after-positive-talks-with-zelensky--f8a9a6da7c99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-us-envoy-witkoff-to-meet-putin-in-russia-after-positive-talks-with-zelensky" /></entry><entry><title>Women lead the charge for Saudi contemporary art</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61e0a221a2d96a7ad00adf0330e468caf9defdfd292a9dbde757ab8f11d02427</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:59:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T09:20:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261021-women-lead-the-charge-for-saudi-contemporary-art--d392ed976421.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261021-women-lead-the-charge-for-saudi-contemporary-art" /><summary type="html">Saudi artists Reem Ali and Bashaer Hawsawi are showing installations that explore the domestic space, feminine spheres and the emotionally charged meaning of the table, in a group show presented by the Villa Hegra as part of the Asia Now art fair in Paris.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>French PM vows stronger security as country prepares for more protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e274c4c2618692984d67ae8c7da8ee8c08648ce97fca3dc6af3a6b881c19e423</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:59:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T09:01:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-pm-vows-stronger-security-as-country-prepares-for-more-protests--fa4b4871d7d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-pm-vows-stronger-security-as-country-prepares-for-more-protests" /><summary type="html">French prime minister Sebastien Lecornu and Interior Minister Laurent Nunez both faced tough questions from members of parliament over the handling of last weekend's violence. Lecornu has promised a massive deployment of police for future protests, while Nunez said the military will be used to back up the security forces. Details by FRANCE 24’s Ellen Gainsford live from the prime minister's office.</summary></entry><entry><title>Italy deploys army and approves tougher anti-riot laws after violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e10ec578eff1734e463fb5636e6d3d7005eead71e8d50b727f87a44e60fe5a17</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:59:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:57:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/italy-deploys-army-and-approves-tougher-anti-riot-laws-after-violence--92b0ab3689c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/italy-deploys-army-and-approves-tougher-anti-riot-laws-after-violence" /><summary type="html">Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni on Tuesday announced the deployment of 500 troops to Milan to assist police following clashes in the city. Meloni said a cabinet meeting also approved measures to make the detention of minors easier and to impose fines on their parents for any damage. Story by Morgan Ayre.</summary></entry><entry><title>Champions League: Paris defeat Barcelona but lose three major players to injuries</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3732d4d7b37d8271e0dd0e7a3bf9671979eeb56c1bf916d8ac1688010618eb92</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:59:10Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:21:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261021-champions-league-paris-defeat-barcelona-but-lose-3-major-players-to-injuries--9daf3ba45836.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261021-champions-league-paris-defeat-barcelona-but-lose-3-major-players-to-injuries" /><summary type="html">Paris Saint-Germain beat FC Barcelona (4-2) and have moved to the top of the Champions League table. However, Ousmane Dembélé, Marquinhos and Khvicha Kvaratskhelia were all forced off through injury.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Russia releases US citizen accused of fighting for Ukraine, Putin says during Witkoff meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcbd702e7ee2f048e2635884a8cb98e268427a0ba93820724ebe926c67c56097</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:58:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T04:29:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-us-envoy-witkoff-to-meet-putin-in-russia-after-positive-talks-with-zelensky--f8a9a6da7c99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-us-envoy-witkoff-to-meet-putin-in-russia-after-positive-talks-with-zelensky" /><summary type="html">US special envoy Steve Witkoff met with Russian President Vladimir Putin in Saint Petersburg on Wednesday after talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky in Oslo. Putin said during the meeting that Russia had released US citizen Stephen Hubbard, who has been imprisoned for years in Russia after being charged of fighting as a mercenary for Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Boeing's 737 Max 10 finally wins FAA approval after years of delays</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b907f00465b320cfd9ac7f482d84bb02f6552baba71daaede79f1847efde13a6</id><updated>2026-10-21T13:57:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T01:11:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20261021-boeing-s-737-max-10-finally-wins-faa-approval-after-years-of-delays--7e75e633c86f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261021-boeing-s-737-max-10-finally-wins-faa-approval-after-years-of-delays" /><summary type="html">Boeing's largest 737 Max jet has cleared a major regulatory hurdle, with US aviation authorities approving the Max 10 for passenger service on Tuesday after nearly a decade of delays. The certification marks a boost for the planemaker's recovery, with deliveries expected to begin in 2027.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry></feed>
